## Project Summary

*AI-generated project summary produced by `/write-summary`, for future AI sessions catching up without re-analyzing line-by-line; may be out of date — re-run to refresh.*

### Purpose

A launcher for pre-made Claude Code agents running in isolated Docker containers. Each agent has distinct instructions, model, and parameters, but shares OAuth credentials, workspace, slash commands, status-line, and memory pointer. Eliminates the friction of re-authenticating and re-configuring Claude Code per persona.

### Tech Stack

- Python 3 (single-file launcher, ~100 lines, no packaging)
- Docker + Docker Compose (one container per launched agent)
- Debian Bookworm slim base; Claude Code CLI installed via `claude.ai/install.sh`
- Python deps on host: `pick` (TUI picker), `python-dotenv` (parse `.conf` files)
- Inside image: `ripgrep` (forced via `USE_BUILTIN_RIPGREP=0`), `git`, `curl`, plus a build toolchain — Rust via `rustup`, `uv` for Python, `python3-pip`/`venv`, `build-essential`, `pkg-config`, `libssl-dev` — so agents can compile native deps
- No tests, no CI, no lockfile

